{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":53677,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"claude-opus-5-5","packSha":"61de395aac3db8f678f5554f99519de183d8b608064c093b680c19fa1700b55b","packTokens":24444,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"platform","tokens":280,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"tpl","tokens":374,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"intent","tokens":1000,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":965,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"assumptions","tokens":3790,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"cb","tokens":1844,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"spec","tokens":16078,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":7,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"critic"},"pointers":[],"system":"PLATFORM. This product is designed and built as a web app, and nothing else. Where the requirements ask for a mobile app, a phone app, an iOS or Android app, treat them as the same features in one responsive web app that works well on a phone's browser: never stop, park, ask or leave a requirement out because it names a mobile app, and never plan a native app, an app store step or a phone-only frame. Every page is responsive: it is laid out for a phone, a tablet and a desktop width, with touch-sized controls on the narrow one. What only a native app can do (push notifications, background location, a home-screen icon) is given its closest web form (an in-app notice or email, the browser's location prompt, an installable web app) and said so.\n\nAdversarial reviewer. Find defects in this spec; don't praise; don't rewrite it.\nRubric: 1 conflicts between requirements 2 missing error, empty and permission paths 3 ACs not observable at a public surface 4 scope creep beyond the intent 5 claims about existing behaviour without anchors 6 state transitions and existing data 7 behaviour changes outside the requested scope (blast radius) 8 hardcoded identifiers that should be configuration.\nEach finding: rubric number, reqId, severity (critical|high|medium|low), one-sentence evidence in \"finding\". Empty list if none.\nThe human answered questions and accepted assumptions (below). Scope they decided is not a defect: don't flag it.\nThis spec is for the web side of a product whose API is a separate service, built and tested from the same request in a run of its own. Behaviour listed out of scope citing API-SIDE is that run's work: don't flag it as missing, and don't flag a criterion for checking a server rule only through what the screen shows.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"intent\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n{\n \"changeClass\": \"feature\",\n \"header\": {\n  \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-12T19:22:06.057Z\",\n  \"inputsHash\": \"\",\n  \"kind\": \"intent\",\n  \"producedBy\": {\n   \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n   \"stage\": \"intake\"\n  },\n  \"runId\": \"20261012-meridian-coldchain-platform-in-9fcb\",\n  \"schemaVersion\": 1\n },\n \"rigor\": \"full\",\n \"risk\": \"high\",\n \"riskTags\": [\n  \"auth\",\n  \"pii\",\n  \"migration\",\n  \"payments\"\n ],\n \"source\": \"cli\",\n \"spans\": [\n  {\n   \"id\": \"I-1\",\n   \"text\": \"Replace the current manual processes with a single platform covering stock, orders, deliveries, live temperature monitoring, quality decisions and recalls.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"I-2\",\n   \"text\": \"Provide a responsive web portal for warehouse staff, dispatchers, quality staff, administrators and auditors.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"I-3\",\n   \"text\": \"Provide a customer portal for hospitals, pharmacies and clinics.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"I-4\",\n   \"text\": \"Provide a driver experience that keeps working without a connection.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"I-5\",\n   \"text\": \"Receive temperature readings from data loggers and cold-room sensors.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"I-6\",\n   \"text\": \"Keep a centralized shared record of stock, orders and temperature history.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"I-7\",\n   \"text\": \"Support secure sign-in, role and warehouse access controls, customer-organization isolation, and read-only auditor access.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"I-8\",\n   \"text\": \"Define versioned product temperature profiles and stability budgets.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"I-9\",\n   \"text\": \"Receive stock by lot, track inbound logger readings, quarantine stock, and release it through quality review.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"I-10\",\n   \"text\": \"Let customer users place, view, change and cancel orders under the specified delivery and order rules.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"I-11\",\n   \"text\": \"Allocate released stock to orders by earliest expiry while respecting shelf-life, availability and order-completion rules.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"I-12\",\n   \"text\": \"Pack stock into qualified shipper boxes and plan routes with drivers and vehicles.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"I-13\",\n   \"text\": \"Store and process delayed, duplicated and out-of-order temperature readings reliably.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"I-14\",\n   \"text\": \"Detect excursions, charge stability budgets, place affected stock on hold, and alert relevant users.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"I-15\",\n   \"text\": \"Enable drivers to load, drive and record delivery handovers using their phone, including offline use.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"I-16\",\n   \"text\": \"Support the portals in English and Arabic, with Arabic displayed right to left.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"I-17\",\n   \"text\": \"Track recalled lots, block remaining stock and account for customer responses.\"\n  }\n ],\n \"touchesUi\": true\n}\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"What must the full two-person quality decision for stock exposed to a not-permitted temperature range require?\",\n  \"answer\": \"A Quality Officer proposes the disposition and a different Quality Manager approves it; neither person can perform both steps.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"When an excursion opens, how quickly must affected stock be placed On Hold relative to the alert deadline?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Place it On Hold as soon as the excursion is detected; the two-minute deadline applies to alerts.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"What customer evidence must the driver record for a delivery handover?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Record the recipient's name and an explicit electronic acknowledgment of receipt; a drawn signature is not required.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"What should happen to quantities that are not handed over because a delivery is refused or only partly completed?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Keep undelivered quantities outstanding; record the reason and return them to available stock only after warehouse receipt and any required quality checks.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"What constitutes a handling unit for tracking stability budgets when a received quantity is split, moved, or packed into different boxes?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Track quantities as handling units and split the record whenever portions acquire different temperature histories.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"Who may maintain a customer organisation's saved delivery addresses and minimum remaining shelf-life requirement?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Customer Administrators maintain their organisation's addresses; System Administrators set its minimum shelf life.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"How should the stock quantity breakdown reconcile with quantity on hand, given that stock can also be On Hold, Rejected, Recalled or Expired?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Treat on-hand as the total and show a mutually exclusive breakdown that includes available, allocated, quarantined and the other stock statuses.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"question\": \"When a product profile changes with an effective date, how should the new profile affect stock already received and its temperature-budget history?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Apply the new version to stock still held from its effective date onward and recalculate affected budgets and decisions from that date.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"assumptions\" kind=\"assumptions\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"fromDefault\": \"offline\",\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-4\",\n   \"I-7\",\n   \"I-15\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-1\",\n  \"risk\": \"high\",\n  \"text\": \"If a driver records actions offline and their account is disabled or removed before synchronization, should those queued actions be accepted into the shared record? → assumed: No; online only.\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-13\",\n   \"I-14\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-2\",\n  \"risk\": \"high\",\n  \"text\": \"How should a temperature-history gap affect stock status and stability-budget calculations? → assumed: Mark exposure as unknown, do not charge a specific temperature tier without a reading, and flag the affected stock for quality review without automatically placing it On Hold.\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-9\",\n   \"I-11\",\n   \"I-17\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-3\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"How should stock in On Hold, Rejected, Recalled, and Expired states appear in the quantity view that must reconcile to on-hand stock? → assumed: Show on-hand as a total and show non-overlapping quantities for available, allocated, quarantined, On Hold, Rejected, Recalled, and Expired stock beneath it.\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-9\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-5\",\n   \"I-8\",\n   \"I-9\",\n   \"I-13\",\n   \"I-14\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-4\",\n  \"risk\": \"high\",\n  \"text\": \"Are the numeric rules not explicitly marked configurable fixed policy values, or should administrators be able to change them? → assumed: Keep the stated values fixed: 15-minute silence, two-minute alert target, 25% remaining-budget alert, three consecutive in-band readings, and 30-day expiry restriction.\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-10\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-3\",\n   \"I-10\",\n   \"I-11\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-5\",\n  \"risk\": \"high\",\n  \"text\": \"Who sets and maintains each customer's minimum remaining shelf-life requirement? → assumed: A System Administrator sets one value per customer organisation; dispatchers and customers cannot change it per order.\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-11\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-9\",\n   \"I-10\",\n   \"I-12\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-6\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"Which local-time convention should govern warehouse cut-offs, working days, delivery dates, expiry-date changes, and route schedules? → assumed: Use the serving warehouse's configured local time zone for its cut-off, working-day, and route rules; display dates and times in the user's local zone with the warehouse zone identified.\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromDefault\": \"data-migration\",\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-12\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-1\",\n   \"I-3\",\n   \"I-6\",\n   \"I-9\",\n   \"I-10\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-7\",\n  \"risk\": \"high\",\n  \"text\": \"What existing spreadsheet and operational data should be brought into the new platform at go-live? → assumed: No; the system starts empty, with seed data for set-up.\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-13\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-5\",\n   \"I-13\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-8\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"What integration contract is available for the logger supplier's gateway, which sends readings in batches? → assumed: Use the supplier gateway's existing documented batch API; Meridian will provide its interface documentation, credentials, and sample payloads.\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromDefault\": \"file-uploads\",\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-14\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-9\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-9\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"Which file format and validation rules apply to the manufacturer's inbound logger file upload? → assumed: Images and PDFs up to 10 MB each, kept in cloud storage.\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromDefault\": \"notifications\",\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-15\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-2\",\n   \"I-4\",\n   \"I-5\",\n   \"I-14\",\n   \"I-15\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-10\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"Which channels should deliver excursion, silence, low-budget, route-change, and stock-change alerts? → assumed: Email only, from fixed templates; no SMS or push.\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromDefault\": \"audit\",\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-16\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-1\",\n   \"I-6\",\n   \"I-7\",\n   \"I-8\",\n   \"I-14\",\n   \"I-17\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-11\",\n  \"risk\": \"high\",\n  \"text\": \"What history must the audit trail preserve when a regulated record is changed or corrected? → assumed: Who created and last changed each record, and when; no full audit trail.\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromDefault\": \"reporting\",\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-17\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-1\",\n   \"I-6\",\n   \"I-9\",\n   \"I-11\",\n   \"I-13\",\n   \"I-17\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-12\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"What operational reports or exports are needed beyond the stock, order, temperature-history, and recall views already described? → assumed: On-screen lists with filters and CSV export; no custom report builder.\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromDefault\": \"browsers\",\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-18\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-2\",\n   \"I-3\",\n   \"I-4\",\n   \"I-15\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-13\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"Which browsers and versions must the responsive portals support? → assumed: The latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari and Firefox.\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromDefault\": \"accessibility\",\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-19\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-2\",\n   \"I-3\",\n   \"I-4\",\n   \"I-15\",\n   \"I-16\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-14\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"What accessibility conformance level is required for the portals? → assumed: WCAG 2.1 AA on the main flows.\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-20\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-17\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-15\",\n  \"risk\": \"high\",\n  \"text\": \"What customer response and evidence are required before a recalled quantity counts as accounted for? → assumed: Record the customer's response, quantity, and stated disposition for each affected delivery; accept the response as accounted for without requiring supporting documents.\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromDefault\": \"volumes\",\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-21\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-2\",\n   \"I-3\",\n   \"I-4\",\n   \"I-5\",\n   \"I-6\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-16\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"What concurrent user and operational-record volumes should be used in addition to the stated 5,000 devices reporting at once and approximately 400 customer organisations? → assumed: Up to 1,000 users and 100,000 records in the first year.\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromDefault\": \"offline\",\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-4\",\n   \"I-7\",\n   \"I-15\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-17\",\n  \"risk\": \"high\",\n  \"text\": \"If a driver records actions offline and their account is disabled before those actions synchronize, what should happen to the queued actions? → assumed: No; online only.\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-9\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-7\",\n   \"I-13\",\n   \"I-14\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-18\",\n  \"risk\": \"high\",\n  \"text\": \"When a logger or sensor has a gap in readings, how should the unknown interval affect stability budgets and stock disposition? → assumed: Do not charge an assumed temperature tier automatically; flag the gap for quality review and keep affected stock On Hold until resolved.\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-10\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-17\",\n   \"I-3\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-19\",\n  \"risk\": \"high\",\n  \"text\": \"What customer response is sufficient to account for recalled units at each organisation? → assumed: Require a quantity reconciliation for the lot, with each quantity recorded as located, used, returned, disposed of or otherwise accounted for.\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromDefault\": \"data-migration\",\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-11\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-1\",\n   \"I-6\",\n   \"I-9\",\n   \"I-13\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-20\",\n  \"risk\": \"high\",\n  \"text\": \"What existing information from the paper records and spreadsheets must be brought into the new platform? → assumed: No; the system starts empty, with seed data for set-up.\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-12\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-5\",\n   \"I-7\",\n   \"I-9\",\n   \"I-13\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-21\",\n  \"risk\": \"high\",\n  \"text\": \"Which logger supplier gateway and integration interface must provide the live readings, and what inbound logger-file format must the receipt workflow accept? → assumed: Use Meridian's existing supplier gateway and its documented interface; accept that supplier's documented inbound logger export format.\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromDefault\": \"notifications\",\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-14\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-2\",\n   \"I-14\",\n   \"I-15\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-22\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"How should staff and drivers receive time-sensitive excursion and route alerts in the responsive web app? → assumed: Email only, from fixed templates; no SMS or push.\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromDefault\": \"sign-in\",\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-15\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-7\",\n   \"I-3\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-23\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"How should customer users receive the one-time code required for the second sign-in step? → assumed: Email and password, with a reset link by email; no social or single sign-on.\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromDefault\": \"audit\",\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-16\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-6\",\n   \"I-7\",\n   \"I-13\",\n   \"I-14\",\n   \"I-17\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-24\",\n  \"risk\": \"high\",\n  \"text\": \"What audit history must be retained when regulated records are corrected or recalculated, and may original values ever be overwritten? → assumed: Who created and last changed each record, and when; no full audit trail.\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromDefault\": \"browsers\",\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-17\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-2\",\n   \"I-3\",\n   \"I-15\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-25\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"Which browsers must the responsive portals support? → assumed: The latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari and Firefox.\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromDefault\": \"accessibility\",\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-18\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-2\",\n   \"I-3\",\n   \"I-15\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-26\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"What accessibility conformance level is required for the portals? → assumed: WCAG 2.1 AA on the main flows.\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-19\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-10\",\n   \"I-12\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-27\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"Which warehouse time zone determines order cut-offs, working days, delivery dates and route times? → assumed: Use the configured local time zone of the serving warehouse for each of those rules.\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromDefault\": \"volumes\",\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-20\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-2\",\n   \"I-3\",\n   \"I-5\",\n   \"I-6\",\n   \"I-13\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-28\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"What minimum usage scale beyond the stated 5,000 reporting devices should the system be designed to support? → assumed: Up to 1,000 users and 100,000 records in the first year.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"cb\" kind=\"current-behaviour\" sha=\"\">\n{\n \"claims\": [],\n \"header\": {\n  \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-12T19:22:21.911Z\",\n  \"inputs